  ...
#   ok   a line comment's contents are blanked and its newline kept
#   ok   a block comment spanning lines keeps every newline, so line numbers do not move
#   ok   a string literal's contents are blanked
#   ok   code AFTER a template literal survives — the defect that reported 18 real tests as empty
#   ok   a template hole is code and keeps its contents; the surrounding text does not
#   ok   nested templates through a hole close in the right order
#   ok   a quote inside a regex literal does not open a string
#   ok   division is not mistaken for a regex
#   ok   a raw string's contents are blanked, delimiters and all
#   ok   a char literal holding a quote does not open a string
#   ok   a lifetime is not mistaken for an unterminated char literal
#   ok   nested block comments close correctly (rust allows them, C does not)
#   ok   an integration test under tests/ counts its assertions with no \#[cfg(test)] present
#   ok   an assertion in production code is not counted as a guard the suite runs
#   ok   a helper is found by what its body does, not by being called ok
#   ok   a file with no failure path at all reports zero sites rather than passing silently
#   ok   the site is the CALLER, not the helper's declaration line
#   ok   the closing tally is recognised as a summary, not counted as a thirteenth guard
#   ok   a FAIL that resolves to no known site is reported unresolved, never guessed at
#   ok   only <script> contents are mutable, and offsets do not move
#   ok   a mutation offset taken from blanked text still names the real bytes
#   ok   a quote inside a regex does not become a referent — the defect that produced " +\\r\\n   "
