# -- measures (values known independently of this implementation) --
#   ok   PNG encode/decode round-trips exactly
#   ok   box-counting: a line is 1.0, a filled plane is 2.0, a Sierpinski gasket is 1.585
#   ok   spectral slope recovers -beta on synthetic f^-beta noise
#   ok   entropy is 0 on a constant image and large on noise; compression tracks the same way
#   ok   centre-crop takes a square from a non-square image
# -- statistics --
#   ok   Holm is a step-down: monotone, and it is NOT Bonferroni
#   ok   the correction is load-bearing: it flips a verdict
#   ok   a permutation p-value can never be 0 and never exceeds 1
#   ok   both rules are two-sided: a shift DOWNWARD is detected too
#   ok   the shuffle actually shuffles
#   ok   the control-subset null is a distribution, not a point
# -- calibration: does a rule that promises p<=x deliver p<=x at rate x --
#   ok   the POOLED rule is calibrated at n_test=7, n_control=20
#   ok   calibration_registered_rule_is_broken — the control-subset rule fires far above nominal
# -- blinding --
#   ok   a corpus with a labelled filename is refused
#   ok   a hash-named corpus is accepted, and an empty one is not
#   ok   the measuring stage cannot be handed a path outside the blind set
#   ok   the child environment is a whitelist and carries nothing about groups
#   ok   the labels are unreadable until the measurements are frozen and hashed
# -- end to end (synthetic images only) --
#   ok   a set that genuinely differs is FOUND
#   ok   the blinded corpus contains hash names and nothing else; measures.json carries no labels
#   ok   the measurement digest is recorded and matches the file on disk
#   ok   one distribution split at random finds NOTHING
#        (rates: pooled 10/200, control-subset 89/200)
#   ok   and the false-positive RATE over 200 splits sits at nominal, which the single split cannot show
# -- refusals --
#   ok   a design that cannot produce a positive at these n is refused before it runs
#   ok   the registered rule is refused as miscalibrated unless the operator says otherwise
#   ok   a duplicate image across the sets is refused
#   ok   a non-PNG is refused with the reason, not silently skipped
#   ok   a plot and a machine-readable report are written
# -- mutation --
#   killed     blinding/enroll-writes-labelled-filenames
#   killed     blinding/corpus-name-guard-disabled
