#   ok   a file that reaches its summary and fails is FAILED, not crashed
#   ok   a file that prints assertions then DIES is CRASHED, not failed
#   ok   exit 0 with no summary is SILENT — indistinguishable from testing nothing
#   ok   a declared EXPECTED-RED file that is red does not fail the run
#   ok   a declared EXPECTED-RED file that goes GREEN fails the run
#   ok   a file that only QUOTES the marker mid-line does not declare itself
#   ok   the marker below the header window does not declare the file
#   ok   a declared canary that CRASHES is reported as crashed, not excused
#   ok   a summary counting ZERO passes is SILENT, not green
#   ok   the middle-dot summary with passes is GREEN, not silent (L058 R2)
#   ok   the middle-dot summary with a failure is FAILED, not crashed
#   ok   the middle-dot summary with ZERO passes but a failure is FAILED, not silent
#   ok   the middle-dot summary counting ZERO of everything is still SILENT
#   ok   the same words with an UNMEASURED separator are not a summary — still SILENT
#   ok   a SILENT file fails the run — rule 2 holds per file, not just per tree
#   ok   node_modules is not walked
#   ok   all three real summary shapes count as completed
#   ok   a MACHINE-BOUND file whose universe is present runs and is an ordinary green
#   ok   a MACHINE-BOUND file whose universe is absent is NOT-RUN and does not fail the run
#   ok   the run prints how many files ran, how many were NOT-RUN, and the rule that decided
#   ok   a file that CRASHED is not counted among the files that ran
#   ok   every discovered file appears in exactly one bucket on the counting line
#   ok   a MACHINE-BOUND file that RUNS and fails is FAILED, not excused
#   ok   a MACHINE-BOUND file that CRASHES is CRASHED, not excused
#   ok   a MACHINE-BOUND file with no gate at all fails as GATE INERT
#   ok   a gate that only honours the runner's flag, and reads no corpus, fails as GATE INERT
#   ok   a NOT-RUN whose assertions PASS under force fails as GATE TOO STRICT
#   ok   a NOT-RUN whose forced run is RED is still NOT-RUN, and the forced result is printed
#   ok   a NOT-RUN on the machine the file calls home is a class error
#   ok   the same file away from home is an ordinary NOT-RUN
#   ok   a MACHINE-BOUND declaration missing root= or home= is a class error
#   ok   a MACHINE-BOUND file that prints no UNIVERSE line is a class error
#   ok   a NOT-RUN with an empty reason is a class error
#   ok   claiming NOT-RUN while ALSO completing a run is a class error
#   ok   declaring BOTH classes is refused rather than resolved by precedence
#   ok   a file that only QUOTES the MACHINE-BOUND marker does not declare itself
#   ok   the MACHINE-BOUND marker below the header window does not declare the file
#   ok   a NOT-RUN mentioned mid-line in output is prose, not a declaration
#   ok   an UNDECLARED file printing NOT-RUN gets no exemption from it
#   ok   CARRIER: the header describes the marker rule the code actually enforces
